  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Three zones – recover goal-side",
  "description": "Split the court into three equal zones with cones along the boards. Each zone has one attacker (blue) and one defender (red), and a goalkeeper stands in the top goal. Two attackers with a ball start at the bottom goal and go into the first zone, making it 3v1.\n\nThe attackers must get through all three zones and finish on goal. When they get into the next zone, everyone – attackers and defenders – may follow. So the defender who has been beaten must run back quickly and get goal-side in the next zone, making the overload smaller. Play behind the goal is allowed, just as in a game.\n\nIf the defenders win the ball they score by putting it in the empty goal where the attackers started. Swap roles after a few attacks. With more than eight players, the rest wait at the bottom goal and come in as new attackers.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Defender: if you are beaten – run back the shortest way towards the goal, not towards the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Get between the ball and the goal before you try to win the ball, with your stick in the passing lane."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Steer the ball carrier towards the boards, away from the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Attackers: use the overload quickly, before the defenders get back."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
